We sit at the small dining table and eat.
The food tastes really fantastic.
We are not talking about our work projects today.
I tell Nele that I feel very comfortable in the city.
I find that Berlin is really my home now.
Nele smiles and pours me water.
"I am very glad to hear that," she says.
Then she asks, "What do you actually do after work?"
I tell her that I play badminton every Thursday.
"The training always starts at half past five," I explain.
Nele asks me who I play with.
I answer her that we have different partners every week.
"But I don't have my own racket yet," I laugh.
"I just rent one at the club."
"That sounds great," says Nele.
"I really like riding the bicycle on the weekend."
"We will definitely ride to the lake together in the summer," she suggests.
I tell her that this is a wonderful idea.
